  "_meta": {
    "updated": "2026-07-18",
    "note": "Feasibility ground truth for Shiny and Shadow/Purified Pokedex categories. shinyReleased/shadowAvailable only ever carry 'true' here -- absence of a key means \"unknown\", not \"false\" (see whyNoFalseEntries). This pass replaces the prior small hand-curated seed with a full parse of Bulbapedia's GO-specific tracking tables (List of Shiny Pokemon in Pokemon GO; List of Shadow Pokemon in Pokemon GO), which log every species/date/event down to the current game date. Cross-referenced against Serebii.net (pokemongo/shiny.shtml, pokemongo/shadowpokemon.shtml): Serebii was a strict subset with zero contradictions in either direction (every dex number Serebii lists, Bulbapedia also lists; Serebii is simply slower to add newly-released entries -- 72 shiny / 29 shadow dex numbers Bulbapedia had that Serebii did not yet, all recent/legendary/mythical species consistent with a slower-updating secondary source). A further spot-check via web search (aggregating Dexerto/GameRant/Sportskeeda/Dot Esports GO-news coverage) independently confirmed two of the still-unreleased edge cases (Zarude, Enamorus) as correctly NOT shiny-released. Consumers (medaldexEngine.isCategoryFeasible) fall back to 'defaults' for any speciesId not listed.",
    "whyNoFalseEntries": "Shiny releases are permanent once live and Shadow-availability additions are also one-directional in practice (Niantic has not been observed to retire a species from either pool), so a 'true' claim, once correct, stays correct forever. A 'false' claim (\"not yet released\") has no such guarantee -- it can flip to true at any future Community Day/event, and this file has no live feed to keep it current, so a stale 'false' would actively mislead a player. Marking those absent (honestly \"unknown, needs data\") instead of 'false' remains a deliberate accuracy-over-completeness tradeoff.",
    "knownGaps": {
      "description": "Dex numbers confirmed shiny-released (and, where marked, also Shadow-available) per Bulbapedia GO tracking tables, but that have NO corresponding id in this project's src/pages/pogoaccs/data/species.json master species list -- so there is no key to attach a flag to. Not fabricated, not omitted by choice; genuinely unrepresentable until species.json gains these entries (out of scope for this pass -- species.json is owned by the pogoaccs feature, not medaldex).",
